@startuml
title Save my sign-up and skills to the database (issue #44)
autonumber
skinparam linetype ortho

actor Student
boundary "Sign-up / Pick skills / Profile\n(signup.html, skills.html, profile.html\n+ GG.api in js/app.js)" as UI
control "API server\n(server/app.js)" as API
control "Student service\n(server/students.js)" as Service
entity "Prisma Client\n(ORM / data access)" as ORM
database "PostgreSQL\n(gitgood)" as DB

note over Student, DB
  Implemented user story: "As a new student, I want my account and the skills I pick
  at sign-up saved to the database so that my profile is still there after the app restarts."
  Runs with `npm start`. On GitHub Pages there is no API, so the screens fall back to localStorage.
end note

== Create the account ==
Student -> UI : Enter UNCC email, username, avatar\nand press Create account
UI -> UI : Client-side checks (UNCC email,\n3–18 character username, password length)
UI -> API : POST /api/students\n{ email, username, avatar }
activate API
API -> Service : createStudent(prisma, body)
activate Service
Service -> Service : validateSignup(body)

alt input is invalid
  Service --> API : ValidationError (field messages)
  API --> UI : 400 { errors }
  UI --> Student : Show the message under each field
else input is valid
  Service -> ORM : student.findUnique(email)\nstudent.findUnique(username)
  activate ORM
  ORM -> DB : SELECT "Student" WHERE email / username
  DB --> ORM : existing rows (if any)
  ORM --> Service : matches
  deactivate ORM
  alt email or username already used
    Service --> API : ConflictError
    API --> UI : 409 { errors }
    UI --> Student : "That email already has an account"\n+ Load my saved account button
  else new student
    Service -> ORM : student.create({ email, username, avatar })
    activate ORM
    ORM -> DB : INSERT INTO "Student"
    DB --> ORM : new row (id, createdAt)
    ORM --> Service : Student
    deactivate ORM
    Service --> API : profile
    API --> UI : 201 { student }
    UI -> UI : Store studentId in local state
    UI --> Student : Go to Pick skills
  end
end
deactivate Service
deactivate API

== Save the chosen skills ==
Student -> UI : Pick skills and press Continue
UI -> API : PUT /api/students/{id}/skills\n{ skills: [...] }
activate API
API -> Service : setStudentSkills(prisma, id, skills)
activate Service
Service -> Service : validateSkills(skills)
Service -> ORM : $transaction
activate ORM
ORM -> DB : find or create "Skill" rows\n(built-in: shared row; custom: owned by the student)
ORM -> DB : DELETE old "StudentSkill" rows\nINSERT new "StudentSkill" rows
DB --> ORM : committed
ORM --> Service : done
deactivate ORM
Service --> API : profile with skills
API --> UI : 200 { student }
UI --> Student : Continue to the first quest
deactivate Service
deactivate API

== After a restart: load the profile ==
Student -> UI : Open Profile
UI -> API : GET /api/students/{id}
activate API
API -> Service : getStudent(prisma, id)
Service -> ORM : student.findUnique(id, include skills)
ORM -> DB : SELECT "Student" JOIN "StudentSkill" JOIN "Skill"
DB --> ORM : student + skills
ORM --> Service : Student
Service --> API : profile
API --> UI : 200 { student }
UI --> Student : Username, avatar and skills\n"Saved in the database"
deactivate API

note over API, DB
  If PostgreSQL is unreachable, Prisma throws a connection error
  and the API answers 503 with a clear message instead of failing silently.
end note
@enduml
